If a patient receives a prescribed-opioid from an additional-prescriber then every clinician should specifically review a state-PDMP-record for the patient and should assess the patient for an overdose-risk from a combined-opioid-dosage and should assess the patient for an overdose-risk from a medication-combination.
If a patient receives an other-controlled-medication from an additional-prescriber then every clinician should specifically review a state-PDMP-record for the patient and should assess the patient for an overdose-risk from a medication-combination.
A medication-combination-example includes an opioid-example and includes a benzodiazepine-example.
